A||N||2||cscougar||Insurance Claim Help!!||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||06-14-2000||12:57 PM||||My son's excellent 1985 2m6 was rear ended yesterday.  It looks like a total but I haven't heard from the other driver's insurance adjuster so you never know.  If it is a total what can I expect as a settlement on a fully loaded 73,000 mile 2m6 that looked like a new car in and out and has a newly rebuilt 6 cyl engine with about 6000 miles on it.  I am just trying to get a handle on what the settlement might look like.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tom88gt||06-14-2000||01:23 PM||||They are going to low ball you, especially on a fiero.  Have reciepts ready for everything.  Don't rush to settle either.  You don't have to accept what they offer.  You can always go to court (you don't need a lawyer).  The adjuster is under a lot of pressure from his boss to settle quickly as he has several cases open at any one time.  The longer your case takes, the more willing they are to compromise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||06-14-2000||01:28 PM||||When my 87 GT was stolen and the thieves ran into something ( I probably don't want to know what!!) they said they were going to write off my car. They wanted to give me $2500 CDN for my GT. I told them where to go, and gave them receipts to all the work I've done to the car, and photos to prove what kind of condition it was in. In my past experiences, with Saskatchewan insurance adjusters anyways, is that you always end up losing out bigtime if they write off the car. How bad is the damage to youur sons car? Is there any mechanical damage to it? If the damage looks repairable, give Bob Steiger a call at Twin-Lakes fiero and get some prices on used replacement parts and take those numbers to the insurance guys, chances are they'll still fix it for you. ||||reg||1
